1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:04,640
Let's deal with plans, because the one
thing worth understanding properly is how

2
00:00:04,700 --> 00:00:05,697
models get counted.

3
00:00:06,907 --> 00:00:09,258
Open Pricing from the nav. Three plans.

4
00:00:09,318 --> 00:00:14,388
Free, Pro, and Pro Plus, with your current
one marked at the top and highlighted in

5
00:00:14,448 --> 00:00:15,048
the grid.

6
00:00:15,804 --> 00:00:18,329
Free is a real plan, not a crippled trial.

7
00:00:18,389 --> 00:00:23,190
Five models, both theme blocks, every
viewer customisation option, and the live

8
00:00:23,250 --> 00:00:24,482
preview in the admin.

9
00:00:24,542 --> 00:00:29,097
For a store with a handful of hero
products, that may be all you ever need.

10
00:00:29,957 --> 00:00:31,852
Pro is nine ninety-nine a month.

11
00:00:31,912 --> 00:00:36,618
It raises the limit to fifty models and
adds the two settings that make a real

12
00:00:36,678 --> 00:00:41,139
difference to presentation — HDR skybox
and environment maps, and material

13
00:00:41,199 --> 00:00:43,522
variants — plus priority email support.

14
00:00:43,582 --> 00:00:48,471
There's a seven-day free trial, so you can
test the limit before paying anything.

15
00:00:49,331 --> 00:00:53,847
Pro Plus is twenty-nine ninety-nine, and
the model limit comes off entirely —

16
00:00:53,907 --> 00:00:54,507
unlimited.

17
00:00:54,501 --> 00:00:59,314
It's the plan for a full catalogue in 3D
rather than a few showpieces, and it also

18
00:00:59,374 --> 00:01:00,740
has the seven-day trial.

19
00:01:01,600 --> 00:01:03,044
Now the important part.

20
00:01:03,104 --> 00:01:07,362
The limit counts distinct model files, not
places a model is used.

21
00:01:07,422 --> 00:01:12,792
If the same glb is attached to a product
and also sits in your library, that is one

22
00:01:12,852 --> 00:01:13,708
slot, not two.

23
00:01:13,768 --> 00:01:15,409
It's the file that counts.

24
00:01:16,269 --> 00:01:20,653
You can see the count on the dashboard, on
the products screen, and here in the

25
00:01:20,713 --> 00:01:25,042
library — always as models in use over
your limit, so there's no arithmetic to

26
00:01:25,102 --> 00:01:25,702
do.

27
00:01:26,070 --> 00:01:29,916
When you hit it, uploads are blocked
rather than silently failing.

28
00:01:29,976 --> 00:01:34,473
The banner shows the breakdown — library
models, product assignments, and the

29
00:01:34,533 --> 00:01:38,319
reminder that overlap counts once — plus a
direct upgrade button.

30
00:01:39,179 --> 00:01:43,031
You'll see the same message if you try to
assign a model to a new product.

31
00:01:43,091 --> 00:01:47,419
Note that replacing the model on a product
that already has one is always allowed —

32
00:01:47,479 --> 00:01:49,851
you're not adding a file, you're swapping
one.

33
00:01:50,711 --> 00:01:53,403
To upgrade, click Upgrade on the plan you
want.

34
00:01:53,463 --> 00:01:55,921
The app hands you to Shopify's own
billing.

35
00:01:56,781 --> 00:01:58,746
This screen is Shopify's, not ours.

36
00:01:58,806 --> 00:02:03,199
It shows the price, the trial length and
the billing interval, and the charge

37
00:02:03,259 --> 00:02:05,454
appears on your normal Shopify invoice.

38
00:02:05,514 --> 00:02:09,560
We never see your card. Approve, and you
come straight back to the app.

39
00:02:10,420 --> 00:02:14,650
Back in the app, the new plan is marked
Active, the Most Popular badge steps

40
00:02:14,710 --> 00:02:17,133
aside, and your limit is raised
immediately.

41
00:02:17,993 --> 00:02:22,533
The dashboard plan tile now shows Pro,
your monthly price, the subscription

42
00:02:22,593 --> 00:02:26,397
status and any remaining trial days, with
a Manage plan button.

43
00:02:27,257 --> 00:02:31,585
Cancelling is one button at the top, and
here's the part worth knowing: it drops

44
00:02:31,645 --> 00:02:34,053
you to Free, but it does not remove
anything.

45
00:02:34,113 --> 00:02:37,508
Your existing model assignments keep
working on the storefront.

46
00:02:37,568 --> 00:02:40,305
Only new uploads beyond the Free limit are
blocked.

47
00:02:41,165 --> 00:02:43,015
That's a deliberate design choice.

48
00:02:43,075 --> 00:02:47,396
A downgrade can never break a live product
page, so you can move between plans

49
00:02:47,456 --> 00:02:50,542
seasonally without any risk to what's
already published.

50
00:02:51,402 --> 00:02:54,711
One video left: where to go when something
isn't behaving.
